=== [HIGH] scheduler.py:8  ZeroDivisionError in average_wait ===
the tests written for this bug pass on the current code, so it was not reproduced; the fix will be unproven
behavior guard: Check that average_wait computes the correct mean for non-empty lists of wait times. (passes on the current code)
Fix ZeroDivisionError in average_wait when waits is empty by returning 0.0.
--- a/scheduler.py
+++ b/scheduler.py
@@ -6,5 +6,5 @@
 def average_wait(waits):
     """Return the mean waiting time, or 0.0 when nobody waited."""
-    return sum(waits) / len(waits)
+    return sum(waits) / len(waits) if waits else 0.0
 
 
